  "description": "This application is for the 2 lights to remain on the downstream side of the Blackfriars Rail Bridge which are located outside the Thames Tideway Development Consent Order (DCO) approved boundaries and consequently requires an additional Town and Country Planning Application to leave them in place. \nThere are two lights on the NR bridge which were installed under the DCO while the works were being undertaken as part of a requirement from the PLA. One light is an arch closure board and one is a warning light for when the Fleet overflow is discharging into the river, the location on the Eastern side to the Blackfriars Rail Bridge is outside the Limits of Land Acquired (LLAU) as set out in the Tideway Development Consent Order.  The lights have been agreed by network Rail to remain in place and are a requirement of the PLA to ensure that the other river users are aware of any potential dangers form the Fleet discharging into the river\n",
